# Promoted from the learning loop (2026-09-19), then reviewed and kept: this
# generalises to a FAMILY of hardcoded-credential assignments rather than a
# single literal. Merges the loop's duplicate secret/quality/iac variants
# (LEARNED-1789653622-4, -1789659500-4, -1789760026-1) into one canonical rule.
# The specific cloud-key names are folded into the key alternation so a
# provider-prefixed key (aws/heroku/private) is still caught.
id: KEUR-SEC-007
title: Hardcoded credential assigned to a key/secret/token/password
category: secret
severity: critical
engine: pattern
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .js .ts .php .rb .py .go .java .env .yml .yaml .json
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)\b(?:heroku[_-]?api[_-]?key|aws[_-]?secret[_-]?access[_-]?key|aws[_-]?access[_-]?key[_-]?id|private[_-]?key|api[_-]?key|secret[_-]?key|access[_-]?token|auth[_-]?token|token|secret|password|passwd|pwd)\s*[:=]\s*["'][^"']{12,}["']
    message: "Hardcoded credential assigned to a secret-like key (CWE-798). Move it to a secret manager or environment variable injected at runtime; never commit the literal value."
confidence: 0.8
fix: "Do not hardcode credentials. Read them from the environment or a secret manager at runtime. If this value was ever committed, rotate it."
